        Medellin is Latin America's premier nearshore tech hub for US time-zone remote engineers. Gigabit symmetrical fiber across premier El Poblado and Laureles coworking spaces reaches <strong>500–920 Mbps</strong> via Claro and Tigo UNE with an ultra-low <strong>48–58ms ping to AWS us-east-1 (Northern Virginia)</strong>. Top-tier hubs guarantee 99.9% uptime with commercial diesel generator backups, all within a comfortable monthly budget of <strong>$1,400 to $2,400 USD</strong>.
      </p>
