      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        4. Power Outage Defense & UPS Inverter Verification: Keeping Remote Pipelines Alive
      </h2>
      <p>
        While Medellin has exceptional baseline power reliability compared to other South American cities, localized storms during the rainy seasons (April–May and October–November) can trigger momentary transformer trips or lightning surge blackouts lasting from 15 minutes to 2 hours.
      </p>
      <p>
        For remote engineers with production on-call duties or client presentation requirements, understanding power resilience tiers is essential:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-6">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-slate-900/60">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-emerald-400 text-base mb-2">Tier 1: Commercial Generator</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">
            Found in class-A office towers (Tinkko, WeWork). Features automatic transfer switches (ATS) that engage diesel turbines within 8 seconds of grid loss, coupled with UPS banks that bridge the gap with zero power drops.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-blue-500/30 bg-slate-900/60">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-blue-400 text-base mb-2">Tier 2: Inverter Battery Banks</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">
            Common in boutique spaces (Circular). Pure sine-wave lithium-ion inverters keep Wi-Fi routers, core switches, and desk monitors running for 4 to 8 hours, though high-draw air conditioning units will shut down.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-slate-900/60">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-red-400 text-base mb-2">Tier 3: No Generator (Cafes)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">
            Neighborhood coffee shops in Manila and Provenza. Total blackout upon municipal failure; local cellular towers become quickly congested, rendering phone tethering unstable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

